WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.602 --> 00:00:10.501
A boardroom is a debate. You give it a topic, and a Chair runs a meeting in which each seat argues from its own point of view, so you hear the other side before you decide.

2
00:00:11.206 --> 00:00:19.313
Open Boardroom in the sidebar and click New boardroom. Write the topic, add a short brief, and choose a format. Here it is a pre-mortem.

3
00:00:24.289 --> 00:00:37.964
The cast always has an Optimist and a Devil's Advocate. Those two seats are fixed and cannot be removed. Add three or four more: personas from the library, your own agents, or a persona cast from a one-line brief.

4
00:00:40.099 --> 00:00:50.808
Suggest a cast lets the Chair propose seats for the topic, and you can save a cast as a room to use again. Set a round cap, a cost limit and a time limit, then click Start.

5
00:00:51.513 --> 00:00:59.150
The first round is sealed. Every seat answers on its own, so nobody copies anybody, and you only see how many answers are in.

6
00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:07.573
Then all the answers are revealed together. The sticky notes the seats add collect on the whiteboard: ideas, risks and decisions.

7
00:01:08.279 --> 00:01:17.815
When only you can decide, the Chair pauses and asks. Type an at sign and a name to make a seat speak first in the next round, choose an option, and click Decide.

8
00:01:22.298 --> 00:01:27.077
The whiteboard is yours too. Add a note, vote for one, and move it to another column.

9
00:01:31.011 --> 00:01:38.798
When you have heard enough, click End session. The Chair writes the minutes: the positions, the disagreements that stayed open, and the whiteboard.

10
00:01:52.171 --> 00:02:00.214
Pull into PRD starts a discovery session that already knows what the boardroom concluded. The minutes are also kept under Documents.

11
00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:09.883
A boardroom costs what its turns cost, and the meters show it as you go. Pause or end it whenever you like.
